/* Isqrt_r: second intermediate level of Isqrt, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step), the
   component BART refines.
   Purpose: replace the universal fact of Isqrt_ord by the fact a binary search establishes at its
   exit, on the two neighbours res and res + 1: the square of res is at most nn, the square of res + 1
   is greater than nn.
   The one argument that is not linear, the monotony of squares on naturals, is made here, away from
   the loop: if res + 1 <= rr then (res + 1) * (res + 1) <= rr * rr, so rr * rr <= nn gives rr <= res.
   It is the only obligation of this level with content. The loop of the next step then never compares
   two squares: it only reads the result of one product.
   No variable: nothing is inherited. */
REFINEMENT
    Isqrt_r

REFINES
    Isqrt_ord

SEES
    Ctx_Isqrt

OPERATIONS

    res <-- isqrt(nn) =
    PRE
        nn : VAL
    THEN
        res :( res : 0..max_ROOT &
               res * res <= nn &
               nn < (res + 1) * (res + 1) )
    END

END
